body:
Hoping this doesn't kick off a round of bikeshedding on the name, but I feel like this is more in line with homebrew's `brew doctor` subcommand. `starship checkup`? `starship preflight`?

One challenge is that starship is unable to tell whether the symbols have printed correctly, so it is up to the user to examine the output and make sure things make sense. That needs to be communicated in the output somehow.

@ucodery For colors, was there any particular set you were thinking of? Starship supports the 16 basic named colors, the 255 ANSI colors, and color hexes. I think displaying all hex colors would be way too much space. Were you thinking the 16 basic colors + any other colors used in the config? Or anything that could be displayed by starship (e.g. evaluate all possible modules, look at their colors, and then display the union of all those?)
